#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git 2.51.1 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:8
msgid ""
"There shouldn't be anything exciting to see here.  This is primarily to "
"flush the \"do you still use it?\" improvements that has landed on the "
"master front, together with a handful of low-hanging, low-impact fixes that "
"should be safe."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since Git 2.51.0"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:16
msgid ""
"The \"do you still use it?\" message given by a command that is deeply "
"deprecated and allow us to suggest alternatives has been updated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:21
msgid ""
"The compatObjectFormat extension is used to hide an incomplete feature that "
"is not yet usable for any purpose other than developing the feature "
"further.  Document it as such to discourage its use by mere mortals."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:24
msgid "Manual page for \"gitk\" is updated with the current maintainer's name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:28
msgid ""
"Update the instructions for using GGG in the MyFirstContribution document to "
"say that a GitHub PR could be made against `git/git` instead of "
"`gitgitgadget/git`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:32
msgid ""
"Clang-format update to let our control macros be formatted the way we had "
"them traditionally, e.g., \"for_each_string_list_item()\" without space "
"before the parentheses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:35
msgid ""
"A few places where a size_t value was cast to curl_off_t without checking "
"has been updated to use the existing helper function."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:39
msgid ""
"The start_delayed_progress() function in the progress eye-candy API did not "
"clear its internal state, making an initial delay value larger than 1 second "
"ineffective, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:42
msgid ""
"Makefile tried to run multiple \"cargo build\" which would not work very "
"well; serialize their execution to work around this problem."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:45
msgid ""
"Adjust to the way newer versions of cURL selectively enable tracing options, "
"so that our tests can continue to work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:48
msgid ""
"During interactive rebase, using 'drop' on a merge commit led to an error, "
"which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:51
msgid ""
"\"git refs migrate\" to migrate the reflog entries from a refs backend to "
"another had a handful of bugs squashed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:55
msgid ""
"\"git push\" had a code path that led to BUG() but it should have been a "
"die(), as it is a response to a usual but invalid end-user action to attempt "
"pushing an object that does not exist."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:58
msgid ""
"Various bugs about rename handling in \"ort\" merge strategy have been "
"fixed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:64
msgid ""
"\"git diff --no-index\" run inside a subdirectory under control of a Git "
"repository operated at the top of the working tree and stripped the prefix "
"from the output, and oddballs like \"-\" (stdin) did not work correctly "
"because of it.  Correct the set-up by undoing what the set-up sequence did "
"to cwd and prefix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:69
msgid ""
"Various options to \"git diff\" that make comparison ignore certain aspects "
"of the differences (like \"space changes are ignored\", \"differences in "
"lines that match these regular expressions are ignored\") did not work well "
"with \"--name-only\" and friends."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:74
msgid ""
"Under a race against another process that is repacking the repository, "
"especially a partially cloned one, \"git fetch\" may mistakenly think some "
"objects we do have are missing, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:78
msgid ""
"\"git repack --path-walk\" lost objects in some corner cases, which has been "
"corrected.  "
"cf. <CABPp-BHFxxGrqKc0m==TjQNjDGdO=H5Rf6EFsf2nfE1=TuraOQ@mail.gmail.com>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:80
msgid "Fixes multiple crashes around midx write-out codepaths."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:84
msgid ""
"A broken or malicious \"git fetch\" can say that it has the same object for "
"many many times, and the upload-pack serving it can exhaust memory storing "
"them redundantly, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:86
msgid "A corner case bug in \"git log -L...\" has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:90
msgid ""
"Some among \"git add -p\" and friends ignored color.diff and/or color.ui "
"configuration variables, which is an old regression, which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:94
msgid ""
"\"git rebase -i\" failed to clean-up the commit log message when the command "
"commits the final one in a chain of \"fixup\" commands, which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:98
msgid ""
"Deal more gracefully with directory / file conflicts when the files backend "
"is used for ref storage, by failing only the ones that are involved in the "
"conflict while allowing others."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.51.1.adoc:99
msgid "Also contains various documentation updates, code cleanups and minor fixups."
msgstr ""
